{"h":2857,"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.062500000101608055,"w":0.051903114318847657,"t":"Test 1","x":0.08477508635566984,"c":1,"h":0.013081395100512871},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","c":1,"w":0.26297576904296871,"x":0.084775091689588272,"y":0.10901162792747676,"h":0.015988371937820545},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","w":0.71799306233723958,"y":0.1468023256054376,"h":0.019047919314086226,"x":0.08650519901272076,"c":1},{"y":0.16715116285636744,"w":0.14705881754557293,"c":1,"x":0.084775089389946601,"h":0.015988371937820545,"t":"Passage 2 below."},{"h":0.024854753466233115,"c":1,"t":"Why we need silence","x":0.3217993094341085,"y":0.20188943263122927,"w":0.25432525634765624},{"h":0.01308139510051276,"t":"C","x":0.084775086239939929,"c":1,"y":0.57558139537956099,"w":0.015570934613545737},{"y":0.75581395373103011,"h":0.017441859689102612,"t":"D","w":0.019031141599019377,"x":0.084775086567849017,"c":1},{"y":0.24562631196350282,"w":0.62975779215494798,"c":1,"h":0.017494751574527623,"t":"Humans are finely attuned to noise, and for good reason. From an evolutionary","x":0.11764705540447987},{"y":0.26308139537660868,"t":"perspective, sounds give us vital information, helping us navigate the world and avoid","x":0.12456748331812245,"w":0.66435984293619788,"h":0.018934000280872665,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.6557093302408854,"x":0.12456748022990326,"y":0.28197674389964855,"t":"danger. To help ensure loud or unexpected noises get the attention they deserve, our","h":0.017533403080272292},{"y":0.30087209309865492,"t":"internal chemistry alters in response to them. Our blood pressure goes up, muscles","x":0.12283736742587631,"w":0.6453287251790365,"h":0.016132805212299872,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.12456747649286219,"t":"tense and glands release hormones that prepare us for fight or flight. In the short","w":0.63148788452148441,"y":0.31831395320173972,"h":0.01758527722368719},{"c":1,"w":0.62975779215494787,"h":0.017584260149048792,"x":0.1228373668201895,"y":0.3372093020432998,"t":"term, this is a good thing. When we are exposed to too much noise over the long"},{"y":0.35304408694296607,"x":0.1245674889626586,"w":0.64186848958333331,"h":0.020643806857942648,"c":1,"t":"term, however, those responses can lead to a multitude of health issues, from sleep"},{"y":0.37354651169195896,"w":0.33737024943033855,"c":1,"t":"disturbance to even cardiovascular disease.","x":0.1245674704771948,"h":0.015988371937820434},{"w":0.60048497517903643,"h":0.019904644527662163,"y":0.40885996571437289,"t":"The World Health Organization has recently designated excessive noise as an","x":0.12449923395729211,"c":1},{"x":0.12456746748233362,"y":0.42722183313573459,"h":0.018999097061958126,"w":0.6211072794596354,"c":1,"t":"'underestimated threat' to public health, and has said that people living in cities"},{"c":1,"h":0.019000114136596302,"x":0.12456747380533149,"t":"such as Mumbai, Tokyo and Buenos Aires are being exposed to far more than the","y":0.44611616489887274,"w":0.63840830485026046},{"w":0.67301035563151046,"x":0.1245674864638653,"h":0.01754764279258092,"t":"recommended 40 decibels of noise at night. A report from the European Environment","y":0.4650104970186606,"c":1},{"x":0.12624232032652041,"t":"Agency concluded that noise was an ongoing and widespread issue in Europe, with at","h":0.020995232840365197,"w":0.66792388916015633,"y":0.48061410527097082,"c":1},{"x":0.12451419787294886,"y":0.49985561100488551,"h":0.01974387732813454,"c":1,"t":"least 1 in 5 people consistently exposed to levels considered harmful to healthẠạẠThere","w":0.66618784586588542},{"t":"are no \"earlids\" that can protect your brain from noise, says Nick Antonio, an acoustic","h":0.020348837861153823,"w":0.68339101155598958,"y":0.51744186013369087,"c":1,"x":0.12456746987850949},{"c":1,"x":0.12456748187350182,"t":"consultant who has contributed to the British and international standards for noise.","w":0.6557093302408854,"h":0.017546625050570808,"y":0.53633720947230912},{"c":1,"t":"The good news is that several cities have been working to turn the volume down. One of","w":0.67483601888020828,"x":0.12452693905698425,"y":0.57369530043408823,"h":0.01904106807508521},{"t":"the first to do so was London. 'By providing recommendations for quieter buses, reducing","h":0.017543574494027547,"c":1,"w":0.68512110392252612,"y":0.59302325553137047,"x":0.124567475666771},{"t":"noise from roads and also controlling noise from aircraft, they were able to make the","h":0.022538672968421936,"c":1,"x":0.1262081090783001,"y":0.60811918678593457,"w":0.64551656087239584},{"x":0.12456747803702493,"c":1,"y":0.62790697658627315,"t":"city quieter,' says Antonio. Other cities have introduced noise-reducing road coatings,","w":0.64878890991210936,"h":0.019048936388724513},{"y":0.64825581367098628,"h":0.017594431562804158,"w":0.65397923787434897,"c":1,"t":"for instance, alongside greenery that muffles sound. Some solutions are more specific:","x":0.12283737062121342},{"w":0.66964497884114582,"t":"Washington DC's ban on petrol-powered leaf blowers came into effect recently, while in","c":1,"y":0.66419643749927981,"h":0.020616440609504183,"x":0.12452325540989838},{"t":"New York City, legislation has been approved to fine people who modify their vehicles","h":0.022072410983919211,"x":0.12621441112287687,"y":0.68273824716490217,"w":0.65760192871093748,"c":1},{"h":0.019040799124245944,"x":0.12456748392492434,"y":0.70188943339980536,"t":"to make them noisier. 'People are seeing the benefits of these more quiet environments in","c":1,"w":0.6799307759602865},{"x":0.12623350121861299,"t":"their cities,' Antonio says. 'I expect we will see much more of this in the future.'","h":0.019705209138094815,"w":0.60220759073893226,"y":0.71944350114477584,"c":1},{"x":0.12283738102010394,"w":0.67993077596028639,"h":0.017536453636815441,"t":"Researchers are also seeking to understand what aspects of silent experiences are most","c":1,"y":0.75717284823846676},{"x":0.12629756738949188,"y":0.77606718006090758,"c":1,"h":0.017537471378825664,"t":"beneficial to our health. One of the best-researched is the flotation tank: a lightproof,","w":0.66608998616536463},{"x":0.1245674898659621,"h":0.017494751574527623,"w":0.65916951497395837,"c":1,"t":"soundproof tank of salt water in which a person floats as a form of deep relaxation.","y":0.7935619315720811},{"h":0.018904503114245186,"x":0.12629759236304455,"y":0.81104651142275574,"c":1,"t":"While some people experience altered perception in the tanks, involving subtle","w":0.61072662353515628},{"y":0.82994186048994123,"t":"humming sounds and visual effects, these effects are benign and do not detract from","w":0.65743942260742183,"c":1,"h":0.018903486039606898,"x":0.12456748583251198},{"h":0.021129896458918718,"t":"the benefits of the experience, says Justin Feinstein, a clinical neuropsychologist. 'When","w":0.68179260253906249,"y":0.84800759991657226,"c":1,"x":0.12623312565249659},{"t":"you don't have external sensory stimuli coming in, the brain tries to fill the void to","w":0.64013839721679688,"x":0.12456747962737968,"h":0.017501871764367904,"c":1,"y":0.86773255785407144},{"x":0.12629758200721294,"w":0.67820068359374996,"t":"make sense of this dark and silent world,' he explains. 'In these tanks, some people can","h":0.017500854689729617,"c":1,"y":0.8866279066943823},{"x":0.12629759033797683,"t":"even hear the sound of their eyes blinking,' says Feinstein. 'But it is the ability to focus","w":0.67301035563151046,"h":0.019007233659064871,"c":1,"y":0.90261627908581177},{"t":"on the breath that helps people reach a relaxed or meditative state.'","w":0.52459431966145842,"h":0.022512626781423628,"y":0.91996420871622608,"x":0.12613319560517483,"c":1},{"x":0.086505190673151433,"c":1,"w":0.022491348584493018,"y":0.96075581401818977,"h":0.01308139510051276,"t":"20"}]}